    "narrative": "LawDog enters today\u2019s slate with **Cal Raleigh** leading the charge, sporting a stellar 78.97 rating. **Cal Raleigh** is our premier play; he benefits from a favorable matchup against Sugano and a significant park factor boost that pushes his ceiling well into the \"Strong\" territory. **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (66.07) and **Bryce Harper** (64.58) also command high confidence, with **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** providing added intrigue; despite a neutral SP matchup, his elite ability to exploit slow deliveries makes him a primary threat for stolen bases\u2014a critical factor in our strategy given the scarcity of speed. **JJ Bleday** (63.38) serves as an excellent secondary option, as the dynamic platoon advantage against Peterson creates the largest single-category boost (14%) for any player on our active roster today.\n\nThe lineup construction faced a tight squeeze at the margins, with **Zack Gelof** (39.57) and **Jung Hoo Lee** (38.51) falling just short of our 40.0 floor. **Zack Gelof** was the most difficult exclusion; despite a base projection that suggests utility, the combination of a tough 2.91 xERA opponent and a disadvantageous matchup against a high-efficiency catcher forced us to prioritize the higher floor provided by **Dylan Beavers** (55.80), whose 16% park factor edge against Misiorowski makes him the safer volume play. We must keep a close eye on the SS slot; while **Jeremiah Jackson** (46.95) is in the starting lineup, his matchup against the elite 2.32 xERA of Misiorowski carries significant risk. With **Will Smith** and **Daulton Varsho** unavailable due to lineup status, we are leaning heavily on the current configuration to maintain our efficiency caps without sacrificing the speed-heavy profile required to gain ground in the standings.",
